    <semantic:process id="_2ee86f26-d02b-4cb4-85a9-5671f2da4119" name="good peer review" triso:readOnly="false" triso:collectEnds="true" isClosed="false">
        <semantic:textAnnotation id="_b87d9ae8-1a28-42dc-a78d-b3d2cb4060ca">
            <semantic:text>Before you share your diagram, check these five essentials:

Start &amp; End Events

Every process must have at least one start and one end.
Verb–Object Task Names

Activities are named like “Submit Request” or “Verify Payment”.
Gateways = Decisions

Gateways only appear when the flow splits or rejoins logically.
Label outgoing paths clearly (Yes / No).
Flows Stay Clean

No crossing sequence flows.
Use message flows only between pools.
One Idea per Diagram

Keep it simple: avoid overloading a single model.
Break out subprocesses if needed.</semantic:text>
        </semantic:textAnnotation>
    </semantic:process>
